WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.810
One sheet of card, twenty
centimetres by thirty.

2
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.290
Roll it one way, edges
just meeting: a tall,

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.370
thin tube, thirty centimetres high.

4
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.380
Roll it the other way: a short, wide tube,

5
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.160
twenty centimetres high.

6
00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.690
Same card, same curved area.

7
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.080
A bag of rice is ready to pour.

8
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.010
Which tube holds more?

9
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.880
In this mission, you'll see that a cylinder
is a prism with a circular cross-section,

10
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.080
so its volume is pi r squared h.

11
00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.540
You'll unroll a cylinder's
curved surface into a rectangle,

12
00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.640
whose width is the circumference.

13
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.160
So the edge of the card that wraps
round decides the radius of the tube.

14
00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.300
Your mission: work out
which tube holds more,

15
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.170
the tall one or the wide one.
